*Documentation System* | V-$CHIPVR ($CHIPCN)

The ChipLang documentation system searches for ''.chpdoc'' files in multiple locations.

*Search Order*

The documentation system searches paths in the following priority order:

1. ''doc/'' - Local development directory
2. ''~/.local/share/chiplang/doc/'' - User-local documentation
3. ''/usr/share/doc/chiplang'' - System documentation (managed by installer)

*Usage*

'''
chippy doc                  # Show index page
chippy doc <document>       # Show specific document
chippy doc list             # List all available documents
'''

*Document Format*

Documentation files use the ''.chpdoc'' extension, which is custom. It is designed for simple rendering to a terminal and supports:

- *Bold text* using the * character
- ''Inline code'' highlighting using double apostrophes
- Version variables ''CHIPVR'' and ''CHIPCN'' (prefixed with ''$'') are expanded automatically
- Code blocks using triple apostrophes with line numbers:
'''
Like
this
'''
I recommend you look at ''/usr/share/doc/chiplang'' for practical examples on how to use ''chpdoc'', it really is very simple.

*Third-party Integration*

Third-party packages can install documentation to ''~/.local/share/chiplang/doc/'' without interfering with system documentation. This directory is not touched by the installer on reinstalls and upgrades. I don't recommend installing your documents to ''/usr/share/doc/chiplang''.
